{
  "dom_id": "step-q336795",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}{e}^{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x]}^{\u2032}}{{[{e}^{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}]}^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{-{csc}^{2}\u2061x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}(-{csc}^{2}\u2061x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\cancel{-{csc}^{2}\u2061x}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}\\cancel{(-{csc}^{2}\u2061x)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
